# Current events in town, part three: newcomers ({subject}) and festivals, today or a few days off ({festival}).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Newcomers

scene et_new_seen
when topic=newcomer
a : There's a new face in town. {subject}, they call them. | Have you met {subject}? Just moved here. | {subject}'s taken a room. Says they're staying.
b[innkeeper] : Paid a month in advance. That's the sort of newcomer I like.
b[old] : New faces come and go. Let's see if this one stays the winter.
b : I've seen them about. | Not yet. What are they like? | Staying? Here? Brave.
a : Seems decent enough. | Quiet. Watchful. | Or desperate.
b?[friends] : We should ask them to supper. It's lonely, being new.

scene et_new_suspicious
when topic=newcomer band=friends|family|spouses
a : I don't trust {subject}. Too many questions. | Where did {subject} come from, really? | {subject} smells of somewhere far off. I don't like it.
b[guard] : I've got my eye on them. Nothing yet.
b : Questions aren't a crime. | Ask them. | You don't like anything new.
a : Not yet. | I might. | That's not true.

scene et_new_welcome
when topic=newcomer
a : I took {subject} a loaf. They looked like they'd not eaten in days. | Showed {subject} the way to the well this morning. | {subject} asked me where the chapel was. Polite sort.
b[priest] : The Bright One asks us to make room. Good.
b : That's kind. | Somebody had to. | That's a good sign.
a : It cost me nothing. | Nobody else would. | I thought so too.

scene et_new_work
when topic=newcomer
a : Is {subject} looking for work? | {subject} asked if anyone's hiring. | I hear {subject} knows a trade.
b[merchant] : I could use a pair of paws, if they can count.
b[farmer] : Harvest needs every back. Send them to me.
b : Everyone is. | Not many are. | Which one?
a : True enough. | No. Sadly. | Nobody's sure.

scene et_new_children
when topic=newcomer a.stage=young|adolescent
a : There's a new wolf called {subject}. Do they have any pups? | {subject} talks funny! | I saw {subject}. They've got a scar on their ear!
b : I don't know. Ask nicely. | Don't say that to their face. | Don't stare at it.
a : I'll ask. | Why not? It's true. | I only looked a little.

scene et_new_old_view
when topic=newcomer a.stage=old
a : Another newcomer. {subject}. This town was all family once. | In my day, newcomers brought a gift to every door. | That {subject} hasn't been to chapel once.
b : Towns grow. | Times change. | Give them time.
a : Too fast. | Not for the better. | Hm.

scene et_new_strangers
when topic=newcomer band=strangers|acquaintances
a : You'll have seen the newcomer. {subject}. | New wolf in town. {subject}. | Someone new's moved in. {subject}.
b : I have. | I heard. | So I gather.
a : That's all I know. | Seems fine. | We'll see.

scene et_new_tavern
when topic=newcomer place=tavern
a : That's {subject}, the newcomer. In the corner. | {subject} bought a round last night. Everyone loves them now. | {subject} sits alone every night.
b[innkeeper] : Pays, drinks slow, no trouble. Best customer I've had in a month.
b : Looks lonely. | Buying friends is still buying. | Somebody ought to sit with them.
a : I'll go over. | Cynic. | Go on, then.

scene et_new_romance
when topic=newcomer a.stage=adult b.stage=adult band=friends
a : Have you seen {subject}? Very handsome. | {subject} smiled at me at the well. | I think I'll need directions from {subject}. Somewhere far.
b : Calm yourself. | Smiled? Or squinted? | You're shameless.
a : I'm perfectly calm. | Smiled. Definitely. | I'm hopeful.

scene et_new_rumour_past
when topic=newcomer
a : They say {subject} left their last town in a hurry. | {subject} won't say where they're from. | I heard {subject} was a soldier once.
b[guard] : Then they'll keep the peace, or I'll know why.
b : Everyone's running from something. | That tells you something. | Could be. They walk like one.
a : True. | It does. | They do.

scene et_new_lost
when topic=newcomer place=street|gate|market
a : {subject} got lost twice today. Kept asking for the same street. | Poor {subject}. The streets here wind like eels. | Saw {subject} reading the signs out loud.
b : We all did, once. | It's a maze. | At least they can read.
a : True. | Worse in fog. | Fair point.

scene et_new_scent
when topic=newcomer
a : {subject} smells of pine. Mountain folk, I'd say. | {subject}'s scent is all road dust and smoke. | You can smell the sea on {subject}.
b[old] : A nose never lies. Scent tells you more than any story.
b : Long way from home, then. | Travelled hard. | A sailor, maybe.
a : Long way. | Very hard. | Maybe.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Festivals today

scene et_fest_today_joy
when topic=festival when=today
a : It's {festival} today! Have you seen the streets? | A merry feast to you, for {festival}! | Ribbons on every door for {festival}.
b[old] : I've seen sixty of them and I still get a flutter.
b[child] : There's going to be dancing and sweets and fire!
b : Like a painting. | And to you! | Ribbons everywhere.
a : Isn't it? | Eat well. | Lovely, isn't it.
a?[friends] : Dance with me later. I won't take no.

scene et_fest_today_work
when topic=festival when=today a.role=merchant
a : Busiest day of the year, this. I've not sat down. | Out of honey cakes already, and it's only noon on {festival}. | Everyone wants something on {festival}.
b : Good for the purse. | Make more! | It's the season for it.
a : Hard on the paws. | With what flour? | It is.

scene et_fest_today_guard
when topic=festival when=today a.role=guard
a : A feast day means drunks. Lots of drunks. | No days off on {festival} for the watch. | Keep an eye out today. Pickpockets love {festival}.
b[guard] : I'll bet you a penny we break up three fights before dusk.
b : Every year. | Never is. | I will.
a : Every year. | Never. | Good.

scene et_fest_today_priest
when topic=festival when=today
a[priest] : On {festival}, we remember the Bright One gave us the hearth and the year's turning. Come to the chapel at noon.
a : Are you going to the chapel blessing for {festival}? | The priest's preaching about {festival} at noon. | Will you light a candle for {festival}?
b[priest] : I'd better. I'm leading it.
b : After the feast. | I'll go for the hymns. | One for each of my family.
a : Ha! | Just the hymns? | A good tradition.

scene et_fest_today_food
when topic=festival when=today place=market|street|tavern
a : Smell the roasting? The feast for {festival}. | I've eaten three pies already. It's {festival}! | Honey cakes for {festival}, free at the hall!
b[cook] : I've been up since the third hour basting. My arms are dead.
b : Can't miss it. | Three! You'll burst. | Free? Run!
a : Follow your nose. | Worth it. | Running.

scene et_fest_today_children
when topic=festival when=today a.stage=young|adolescent
a : It's {festival}! Can I stay up late? | Can we go see the fire? Please? | I got a ribbon for {festival}!
b : Just this once. | After supper. | It suits you.
a : Yes! | Promise? | I know.

scene et_fest_today_lonely
when topic=festival when=today band=friends
a : It's my first feast day without my mother. | It isn't the same this year, the feast. | I don't feel much like {festival}.
b : Then spend it with us. | Nothing's the same. | You don't have to.
a : Thank you. | No. | I know.

scene et_fest_today_weather_bad
when topic=festival when=today weather=rain|storm|snow
a : Rain on {festival}. Of course. | The bonfire won't light in this. | All soaked through, and it's {festival}.
b : Dance in the puddles. | It'll light. It always does. | Wet and happy.
a : Why not. | Hope so. | Mostly wet.

scene et_fest_today_weather_fine
when topic=festival when=today weather=clear
a : Clear skies for {festival}. The Bright One's smiling. | Not a cloud. Perfect for {festival}. | Dry as a bone for {festival}. Bonfire will be huge.
b : For once. | Perfect. | Stand back from it.
a : For once. | Perfect. | Ha!

scene et_fest_today_tavern
when topic=festival when=today place=tavern
a : Another round for {festival}! | Half the town's in here for {festival}. | Somebody's singing the {festival} song. Badly.
b[innkeeper] : At this rate I'll be retiring after {festival}.
b : Just one more. | And the other half's outside. | Very badly.
a : One more. | Every year. | Join in!

scene et_fest_today_old
when topic=festival when=today a.stage=old
a : The feast was grander when I was young. | My mother made a cake for {festival} as big as a cartwheel. | I've danced at fifty feast days. Not today. My hips.
b : Everything was. | Did she? | Fifty! Sit and watch.
a : It was. | Bigger. | I will.

scene et_fest_today_spouses
when topic=festival when=today band=spouses
a : Do you remember our first feast day together? | You still owe me a dance from last year's feast. | Wear the blue sash for {festival}.
b : You fell in the river. | Do I? | The blue one? Fine.
a : I was pushed. | You do. | It suits you.

scene et_fest_today_rivals
when topic=festival when=today band=rivals
a : It's {festival}. Truce for a day? | Even on {festival} you look sour. | Let's not quarrel on {festival}.
b : One day. | You bring out the sour in me. | Agreed. Tomorrow, though.
a : One day. | Charming. | Tomorrow.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Festivals soon

scene et_fest_soon_prepare
when topic=festival when=soon
a : Nearly time for {festival}. Have you got your ribbons? | Only a few days to {festival}. | Everyone's busy getting ready for {festival}.
b[cook] : I've a list of dishes as long as my tail.
b[merchant] : Stocking up. Folk spend on {festival} like coin grows on trees.
b : Not yet. | So soon? | I've done nothing.
a : Better hurry. | Soon. | Me neither.

scene et_fest_soon_child
when topic=festival when=soon a.stage=young|adolescent
a : How many sleeps until {festival}? | I can't wait for {festival}! | Are there fireworks at {festival}?
b : A few more. | Nor can I. | Bonfires. Big ones.
a : Too many. | Really? | Yes!

scene et_fest_soon_doubts
when topic=festival when=soon
a : A feast? With prices what they are? | Time for {festival} already? | I can't afford {festival} this year.
b : Still. A feast is a feast. | Already. | Nobody can.
a : I suppose. | The year flies. | We'll manage.

scene et_fest_soon_dress
when topic=festival when=soon band=friends
a : What are you wearing for {festival}? | I'm having a new sash made for {festival}. | I'll brush my coat till it shines for {festival}.
b : Whatever's clean. | Fancy! | You'll look like a lord.
a : Ha! | I know. | That's the plan.

scene et_fest_soon_hall
when topic=festival when=soon a.job=official|noble|priest
a : The hall's paying for the {festival} bonfire this year. | Have the {festival} ribbons come yet? | We'll need the watch doubled for {festival}.
b : Generous. | Not yet. | I'll tell the captain.
a : Isn't it. | Chase them. | Good.

scene et_fest_soon_strangers
when topic=festival when=soon band=strangers|acquaintances
a : It'll soon be {festival}. | Will you be out for {festival}? | Only a few days to {festival}, I hear.
b : So it is. | Likely. | So I hear.
a : Good. | Perhaps I'll see you. | Should be lively.
